From 3c82e945a2eda6408a12176b247e6e60ae7edaf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joakim Hansson <joakim.hansson87@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:23:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/36] vulkan: fuse elementwise epilogs into mat-vec
 dispatches

Extend the existing mat-vec fusion_flags mechanism with SCALE (constant,
pre/post), SILU, SIGMOID, and elementwise MUL epilogs, applied at the
shader write-back in reduce_result(). New ggml_vk_can_fuse_mmv_epilog
matches MUL_MAT + {SCALE|UNARY(SILU/SIGMOID)|SCALE|MUL} chains (mat-vec
route only), and the dispatch walks the fused chain to set flags, the
folded scale constants, and the mul operand buffer.

The graph_optimize parallelism sort scattered these chains: whitelist the
fusable dependent pairs, and follow a fusable chain past the scan-window
edge so it is never split across sets.

qwen4exp: build the hyper-connection combine gate 2*sigmoid(x/hc) right
after the inject mat-vec (identical math, earlier in the graph) so the
whole chain fuses into one dispatch.

Per decode token this removes ~430 kernel launches (3554 -> 3119) on the
launch-gap-bound Qwen3.8-Flash-Next decode: 96x MUL_MAT+SCALE+SILU, 96x
MUL_MAT+SIGMOID+MUL, 95x MUL_MAT+SCALE+SIGMOID+SCALE, plus shared-expert
gates. Measured on Strix Halo (gfx1151, RADV): plain decode 25.5 -> 26.9
t/s shallow, 23.2 -> 23.9 t/s at 8k; prefill +4% at 8k. Greedy outputs
verified within the run-to-run FP noise floor (logprob delta 0.30 vs 0.46
floor from execution-order variation alone).

